s  dexter tries to explain away the grisly  tableau deb doesn't believe him but  helps him set a fire to cover up their  involvement in marshall's death anyway  eagle-eyed laguerta has been mildly  suspicious of dexter for some time and  her spidey sense goes haywire when she  finds a blood slide at the scene of the  crime matching the bay harbor butcher's  mo by the end of the episode deb finds  dexter's bloodslides and asks him point  blank  are you a serial killer  yes  this is a vital moment in both deb and  dexter's narrative arcs one that shapes  new tragedies on the way  you'd think that if you were an escaped  and most wanted serial killer with a  well-known face you'd stay away from the  place you were apprehended  if you must go back you'd probably  change your appearance for protection  that's just common sense right well here  lies one of the many problems with dress  code hannah mckay is back and still  wanted by the police yet she's done  absolutely nothing to disguise herself  she doesn't even bother to change her  hair color brave of her to be walking  around miami like that  it's a distractingly stupid detail among  several others that make this convoluted  episode terrible deb gets deep into soap  opera territory as it's clear her boss  is in love with her and acting like a  jealous boyfriend meanwhile deb's ex  quinn is pulling away from his  girlfriend jaime who is also angel's  sister and dexter's nanny this web of  relationships is uncomfortably tangled  and only getting worse  the penultimate episode of season 4 is a  nail-biter as arthur mitchell quietly  discovers who kyle butler actually is a  miami metro pd blood spatter analyst  named dexter morgan suspicious that kyle  might not be who he says he is arthur  seeks out other kyle butlers in town  with murderous results eventually the  trinity killer casually strolls through  miami metro even stopping to admire the  murder board chronicling all his crimes  before coming face to face with dexter  and calling him by his true name hello  [Music]  dexter  morgan this is also the episode when deb  discovers quinn's girlfriend is actually  trinity's estranged daughter and the one  who killed deb's boss and lover special  agent frank lundy it's one of the most  tense episodes of the series and that's  why it's one of the best  the introduction of dr evelyn vogel in  the show's final season undoes much of  what we thought we knew about dexter and  harry morgan we find out that dr vogel  knew harry and helped him develop the  code that shapes dexter making dr vogel  dexter's spiritual mother  the episode goes on to reveal that the  brain surgeon is actually dr vogel's son  who faked his own death as a teenager  and has been living under the name  oliver saxon  when dexter pulls a fast one and tries  to trap the brain surgeon saxon gets  away by the end of the episode we  learned that dr vogel might have been  working with saxon all along a double  cross that doesn't make sense this is  one of the show's weakest episodes when  it should be one of the strongest  john lithgow's tour de force performance  as the trinity killer has several high  notes in this episode in order to figure  out just how such a prolific serial  killer could also be an exceptional  family man dexter stalks arthur mitchell  in the process dexter finds out that  arthur is violent and abusive toward his  family behind closed doors dexter begins  to regret saving arthur when he tries to  kill himself  little does dexter know he'll regret a  whole lot more before the season is up  hungry man features a key thanksgiving  dinner where rita ends up kissing their  neighbor elliot which turns into its own  drama while rita is kissing elliott  dexter is pretending to be kyle butler  at arthur mitchell's house  he gets into a confrontation with arthur  as he tries to protect the mitchells  after arthur breaks his son's finger for  damaging his car it's a harrowing  tightly written episode that hints at  the devastation the season's finale will  bring  the pen ultimate episode of dexter is a  shocker but not in a good way  calling back to the show's popular  trinity killer arc dexter attempts to  double-cross oliver saxon by pretending  to be on his side it almost works but  what does dexter do instead of killing  the man he's been hunting this entire  season  he leaves him alive and calls deb to  arrest him instead  saxon manages to stab clayton the bounty  hunter steal his gun then shoot deb  square in the stomach it's a terrible  way to end the story of deborah morgan  one of the show's most fascinating and  three-dimensional characters  from the very beginning the one person  who suspects dexter morgan is hiding a  terrible secret under his personable  veneer is sergeant james doakes by  episode 9 of season 2 dokes finally  figures it all out dexter morgan is the  bay harbor butcher but like almost  everyone who figures out the truth about  dexter doakes leaves just enough  evidence behind for dexter to spin in  this case dexter's trophy blood slides  in the trunk of doke's car makes room  for miami metro to suspect dokes  while dokes proves to be one of the most  brilliant characters on the show being  the first to id dexter this hour marks  the beginning of doke's untimely end  the tension between dexter and dokes is  extraordinary by this point and the plot  twists are orchestrated for maximum  effect  the vogel and saxon drama continues in  this episode as dr vogel tries to rein  in her psychopathic son the traumas that  turned young daniel vogel into the brain  surgeon are revealed which land oddly  when counterbalanced by dexter planning  to move to argentina with hannah and  harrison things get especially weird  when hannah who still looks exactly the  same as her wanted poster is recognized  by a receptionist at a hospital yes this  increases the tension but in an annoying  way that makes you shake your head  rather than feel nervous for dexter and  his family in the meantime the dab and  quinn drama continues as quinn breaks up  with jaime who verbally assaults deb  right in the middle of miami metro it's  embarrassing to watch  sergeant doakes may have died at the end  of season 2 but his ghost remains very  much present especially once laguerta's  suspicions about dexter start to bear  fruit  dokes died with people believing he was  the bay harbour butcher and laguerta  sees a much desired opportunity to clear  his name when dexter goes after hector  estrada another key player in his  mother's murder dexter concocts an  elaborate plan to frame estrada for  laguerta's murder  in this heart-pounding finale deb  figures out dexter's plan and arrives  just in time for laguerta to wake up  from the sedative she begs deb to kill  dexter or arrest him  but since deb's feelings for dexter have  been revealed to be much more  complicated than a sister's simple love  for her adopted brother she instead  saves dexter and murders innocent  laguerta in cold blood who am i  is this a new beginning  or the beginning of the end  the series finale is consistently listed  as one of the worst endings of all time  instead of being able to say a proper  goodbye to dexter we spend this last  hour watching deb die  after trying to kill deb once more in  the hospital saxon is arrested and  dexter proceeds to kill him in the  police station with a pen dexter sends  hannah off with his son to buenos aires  where he insists he will meet them all  the while a huge hurricane approaches  miami prompting dexter to take deb off  life support and dump her body where he  used to unload his kills before riding  into the storm absolutely none of this  makes sense the last we see of dexter  finds him living as a lumberjack in  oregon it's a dreadful and unsatisfying  ending for everyone's favorite anti-hero  but then again should serial killers get  happy endings check out one of our  newest videos right here plus even more  looper videos abou